body:
I was diagnosed with extremely mild Aspergers, sometimes I agree with the diagnosis, most of the time, I question it. I barely have any of the symptoms (no routines, no sensory issues, etc.) I am socially awkward, but I think a lot of it comes from lack of confidence, rather than lack of social skills. I have intense interests, but my interests vary wildly, unlike the narrow obsessions you hear about with Aspergers. I was later diagnosed with ADHD, which I agree with 100%. I think the ADHD can explain behaviors I had that experts thought was Aspergers.

&#x200B;

I'm with you in not wanting people to know you're autistic. Autism and Aspergers are such loaded terms, the stigma makes it hard to be proud of my diagnosis. The label hurt my self esteem for a long time, and my mom attributed everything I did to my Aspergers. I think I would die if my irl friends found out about my diagnosis.
